def _claim(self, operation_id: str, blocking: bool):
    """Hold the cross-process attempt claim for one operation.

    The fcntl exclusive lock on ``operation-artifacts/<id>.lock`` is held
    for the WHOLE first-provider-call..terminal window: a concurrent
    HTTP/CLI retry (any thread or process) can only take the attempt over
    once the original owner is truly gone, never while it is minting
    handles. ``blocking=False`` yields None immediately when another owner
    holds the claim (used by retries, which then wait on the terminal like
    any same-key waiter); ``blocking=True`` is used by the single binding
    winner. Raises ArtifactStrandUnavailable when the claim itself cannot
    be taken for a storage reason.
